<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>PROOFS</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proofs for <a href="#S4" title="4 THE THEORY OF INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Characterisation of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any prior <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math> and any non-positive reward function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(a,s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(a,s)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have simple expressions for the soft <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> functions given by:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{\pi}(a_{t},s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{\pi}(a_{t},s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex44.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we define the auxiliary <em id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">optimality variables</em> <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> to have Bernoulli distributions with:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t}=1|s_{t},a_{t})=e^{r(s_{t},a_{t})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t}=1|s_{t},a_{t})=e^{r(s_{t},a_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this by backward induction. Base case <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{\pi}(s_{T},a_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{\pi}(s_{T},a_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r(s_{T},a_{T})=\log(\exp r(s_{T},a_{T}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r(s_{T},a_{T})=\log(\exp r(s_{T},a_{T}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{T}=1|s_{T},a_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{T}=1|s_{T},a_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">and:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi}(s_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi}(s_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(a_{T}|s_{T})}\left[{\exp Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{T})}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(a_{T}|s_{T})}\left[{\exp Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{T})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(a_{T}|s_{T})}\left[{p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{T}=1|s_{T},a_{T}}\right])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(a_{T}|s_{T})}\left[{p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{T}=1|s_{T},a_{T}}\right])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{T}=1|s_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{T}=1|s_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, assuming that the hypothesis holds for <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;t^{\prime}\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;t^{\prime}\leq T</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute for <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{\pi}(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{\pi}(</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex51.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle s_{t},a_{t})=r(s_{t},a_{t})+\log\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}\left[{\exp(V^{\pi}(s_{t+1})}\right])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle s_{t},a_{t})=r(s_{t},a_{t})+\log\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}\left[{\exp(V^{\pi}(s_{t+1})}\right])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log(p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t}=1|s_{t},a_{t})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}\left[{p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}|s_{t+1})}\right])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log(p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t}=1|s_{t},a_{t})\cdot\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}\left[{p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}|s_{t+1})}\right])</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t}=1|s_{t},a_{t})\cdot p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}|s_{t+1},a_{t+1})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t}=1|s_{t},a_{t})\cdot p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}|s_{t+1},a_{t+1})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and the proof of the inductive step for <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as the base case shown above.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In case of deterministic dynamics, we have that <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(\xi|\mathcal{O}_{1:T})=\hat{p}(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\xi|\mathcal{O}_{1:T})=\hat{p}(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We compute the policy for time steps <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle p(a_{t}|s_{t},\mathcal{O}_{t:T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(a_{t}|s_{t},\mathcal{O}_{t:T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|a_{t},s_{t})p(a_{t}|s_{t})}{p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|a_{t},s_{t})p(a_{t}|s_{t})}{p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t+1})p(a_{t}|s_{t})}{p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t+1})p(a_{t}|s_{t})}{p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p(a_{t+1}|s_{t+1},\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T})=\frac{p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}|a_{t+1},s_{t+1})p(a_{t+1}|s_{t+1})}{p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}|s_{t+1})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a_{t+1}|s_{t+1},\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T})=\frac{p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}|a_{t+1},s_{t+1})p(a_{t+1}|s_{t+1})}{p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}|s_{t+1})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, considering <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\hat{p}(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\hat{p}(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math> we have telescoping series:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\hat{p}(\xi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\hat{p}(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t},a_{t})-\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t})+\log p(a_{t}|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t},a_{t})-\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t})+\log p(a_{t}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex59.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log(\mathcal{O}_{T:T}|a_{T},s_{T})-\log p(\mathcal{O}_{1:T}|s_{1})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p(a_{t}|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log(\mathcal{O}_{T:T}|a_{T},s_{T})-\log p(\mathcal{O}_{1:T}|s_{1})+\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p(a_{t}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is exactly:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log p(\xi|\mathcal{O}_{1:T})=\log p(\mathcal{O}_{1:T}|\xi)-\log(\mathcal{O}_{1:T})+\log p(\xi)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p(\xi|\mathcal{O}_{1:T})=\log p(\mathcal{O}_{1:T}|\xi)-\log(\mathcal{O}_{1:T})+\log p(\xi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given deterministic dynamics <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> and policy <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math> and an order-respecting <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{|A|}\to\Delta(|A|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{|A|}\to\Delta(|A|)</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> having a unique maximum, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is an <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max</annotation></semantics></math> indicator, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent if and only if it is greedy w.r.t. its own soft‑<math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> function.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first show argmax necessity under order‑respecting <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>: let <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{|A|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{|A|}</annotation></semantics></math> have a unique maximizer <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=\arg\max_{i}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=\arg\max_{i}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is order‑respecting and outputs a point mass at <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\delta_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\delta_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, suppose <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)=\delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)=\delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq m</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{m}&gt;x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{m}&gt;x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, but the last condition in the order‑preservation definitoin demands <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{m}(x)\geq f_{i}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{m}(x)\geq f_{i}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, a contradiction.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, the forward direction. Assume <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent, and fix the state <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi}(s,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi}(s,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> has a unique maximizer, from what we proved above we know that <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Q^{\pi}(s,\cdot))=\delta_{\arg\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Q^{\pi}(s,\cdot))=\delta_{\arg\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e. <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(s)</annotation></semantics></math> must be an argmax. If there are ties, coherence still forces <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(s)</annotation></semantics></math> to be one of the maximizers, which is consistent with the selector’s tie‑break, as otherwise the per‑state <span id="A1.SS1.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">KL</span> contributes <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. So <math id="A1.SS1.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(s)\in\arg\max Q^{\pi}(s,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(s)\in\arg\max Q^{\pi}(s,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the reverse direction, if <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(s)\in\arg\max_{a}Q^{\pi}(s,a))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(s)\in\arg\max_{a}Q^{\pi}(s,a))</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, we pick <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> to be the <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max</annotation></semantics></math> selector <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Q_{\pi}(s,\cdot))=\delta_{\pi(s)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Q_{\pi}(s,\cdot))=\delta_{\pi(s)}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{KL}(\pi||\pi^{Q,f})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{KL}(\pi||\pi^{Q,f})=0</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition 4.7. ‣ 4.1 Incoherence ‣ 4 THE THEORY OF INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>, i.e., <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS1.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The policy <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{B}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>T</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{B}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-coherent.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove by backwards induction that <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(s_{t}|a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(s_{t}|a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed in iteration <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> and does not change afterwards. In the base case <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> function <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi}(s_{T},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi}(s_{T},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, so it is fixed in the first iteration and remains unchanged. The inductive case follows because <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(s_{t}|a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(s_{t}|a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> only depends on future times <math id="A1.SS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\prime}&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\prime}&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.5</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given any prior <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a policy <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math> such that we have convergence in distribution:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\delta\to 0}\pi^{\delta}\to\pi^{*}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>δ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\delta\to 0}\pi^{\delta}\to\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>δ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined with respect to the soft Q function induced by the prior <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, the policy <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> can be explicitly characterised as the uniform distribution over <math id="A1.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}:=\{a^{*}\in A:Q^{\pi}(s,a^{*})=\max_{a\in A}Q^{\pi}(s,a)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}:=\{a^{*}\in A:Q^{\pi}(s,a^{*})=\max_{a\in A}Q^{\pi}(s,a)\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let us denote <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{*}:=\{a^{*}\in A:Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})=\max_{a\in A}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{*}:=\{a^{*}\in A:Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})=\max_{a\in A}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}^{*}\in A^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}^{*}\in A^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> arbitrarily chosen. 
<br class="ltx_break">For any <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math> we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\delta\to 0}\pi^{\delta}(a_{t}^{*}|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>δ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\delta\to 0}\pi^{\delta}(a_{t}^{*}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex62.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\frac{\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t}^{*})\right)}{\sum_{a\in A}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\frac{\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t}^{*})\right)}{\sum_{a\in A}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\frac{\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)}{\sum_{a\in A}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\frac{\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)}{\sum_{a\in A}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\frac{1}{\sum_{a\in A}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\frac{1}{\sum_{a\in A}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the denominator now splits into:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\delta\to 0}\sum_{a\in A_{t}^{*}}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)=|A^{*}_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\delta\to 0}\sum_{a\in A_{t}^{*}}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)=|A^{*}_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\delta\to 0}\sum_{a\in A\backslash A_{t}^{*}}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\delta\to 0}\sum_{a\in A\backslash A_{t}^{*}}\exp\left(\frac{1}{\delta}Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a)-Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a^{*})\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">giving <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\delta}(a|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>δ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\delta}(a|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> uniform on <math id="A1.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.6</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">A necessary condition for policy <math id="A1.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math> to be optimal is that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\delta\to 0}\kappa_{\delta}(\pi)&lt;\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\delta\to 0}\kappa_{\delta}(\pi)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">From <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem12" title="Definition 4.12 (Boltzmann incoherence). ‣ 4.1 Incoherence ‣ 4 THE THEORY OF INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.12</span></a>, <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Proposition 4.7. ‣ 4.1 Incoherence ‣ 4 THE THEORY OF INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a> and  <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem13" title="Proposition 4.13. ‣ 4.1 Incoherence ‣ 4 THE THEORY OF INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.13</span></a>, we write:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{\delta\to 0}\kappa_{\delta}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{\delta\to 0}\kappa_{\delta}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\text{KL}_{\tau}(\pi(\tau)|\pi^{\delta}(\tau))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mtext>KL</mtext><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>δ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\text{KL}_{\tau}(\pi(\tau)|\pi^{\delta}(\tau))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t}\sim d^{t}_{\pi}}\text{KL}(\pi(\cdot|s_{t})||\pi^{\delta}(\cdot|s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>δ</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lim_{\delta\to 0}\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t}\sim d^{t}_{\pi}}\text{KL}(\pi(\cdot|s_{t})||\pi^{\delta}(\cdot|s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t}\sim d^{t}_{\pi}}\text{KL}(\pi(\cdot|s_{t})||\lim_{\delta\to 0}\pi^{\delta}(\cdot|s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msup><mi>π</mi><mi>δ</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t}\sim d^{t}_{\pi}}\text{KL}(\pi(\cdot|s_{t})||\lim_{\delta\to 0}\pi^{\delta}(\cdot|s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t}\sim d^{t}_{\pi}}\text{KL}(\pi(\cdot|s_{t})||\pi^{*}(\cdot|s_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{t=1}^{T}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t}\sim d^{t}_{\pi}}\text{KL}(\pi(\cdot|s_{t})||\pi^{*}(\cdot|s_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for any <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}\sim d^{t}_{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}\sim d^{t}_{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\text{KL}(\pi||\pi^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{KL}(\pi||\pi^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> is finite if and only <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{supp}(\pi^{*})\subseteq\text{supp}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mtext>supp</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{supp}(\pi^{*})\subseteq\text{supp}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>. Meaning that <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> must assign positive mass to every action in <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. But this is a necessary condition for optimality (by backwards induction on <math id="A1.SS1.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proofs for <a href="#S5" title="5 REMOVING INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition A.7</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Strong return improvement lemma)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The sequence of policies <math id="A1.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i})_{i=0,1,\dots}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i})_{i=0,1,\dots}</annotation></semantics></math> given by the control-by-inference improves its return monotonically, that is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex72" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i+1})\geq J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i+1})\geq J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">We prove this by backwards induction on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>. First, fix some index <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and denote for brevity:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i}\qquad\pi^{\prime}=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i+1}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i}\qquad\pi^{\prime}=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">We also define the future probability of success in a state <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as in <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 4.1 (Soft 𝑄 and 𝑉 functions). ‣ 4 THE THEORY OF INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V^{\pi}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V^{\pi}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex74.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t},a_{t})=r(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p_{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t},a_{t})=r(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Now, we proceed by induction to show that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\pi^{\prime}}(s_{t})\geq V^{\pi}(s_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi^{\prime}}(s_{t})\geq V^{\pi}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">The policy <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}=\mathcal{G}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}=\mathcal{G}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> can be written from Bayes theorem as:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\prime}(a_{t}|s_{t})=\frac{\pi(a_{t}|s_{t})\exp Q^{\pi}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\prime}(a_{t}|s_{t})=\frac{\pi(a_{t}|s_{t})\exp Q^{\pi}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Now:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[\left(\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})\right)^{2}\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>exp</mi><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[\left(\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})\right)^{2}\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>π</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\pi}(a|s_{t})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">where the first line follows from <a href="#A1.E1" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Proofs for ‣ Appendix A PROOFS" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, and the second line follows from Cauchy–Schwarz inequality.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, assume <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi}(a_{T}|s_{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi}(a_{T}|s_{T})</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> and is simply given by <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. We then immediately have from <a href="#A1.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Proofs for ‣ Appendix A PROOFS" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V^{\pi^{\prime}}(\mathcal{O}_{T:T}|s_{t})\geq V^{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{T:T}|s_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\pi^{\prime}}(\mathcal{O}_{T:T}|s_{t})\geq V^{\pi}(\mathcal{O}_{T:T}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">establishing the base of the induction. For the inductive case <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math>, assumethat the above holds for all <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;t^{\prime}\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;t^{\prime}\leq T</annotation></semantics></math> and write:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp V^{\pi^{\prime}}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp V^{\pi^{\prime}}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex78.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=p_{\pi^{\prime}}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=p_{\pi^{\prime}}(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}=1|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[e^{r(s_{t},a_{t})}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}\exp V^{\pi^{\prime}}(s_{t+1})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mi>exp</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[e^{r(s_{t},a_{t})}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}\exp V^{\pi^{\prime}}(s_{t+1})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[e^{r(s_{t},a_{t})}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}\exp V^{\pi}(s_{t+1})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mi>exp</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[e^{r(s_{t},a_{t})}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}\exp V^{\pi}(s_{t+1})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[\exp Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>exp</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi^{\prime}(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[\exp Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[\exp Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>exp</mi><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}\left[\exp Q^{\pi}(s_{t},a_{t})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp V^{\pi}(s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp V^{\pi}(s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where the first inequality comes from the inductive hypothesis, and the second from <a href="#A1.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ A.2 Proofs for ‣ Appendix A PROOFS" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
From the Cauchy–Schwarz, inequalities are strict unless <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\pi}(s_{t},\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\pi}(s_{t},\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi(\cdot|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\cdot|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>-almost-surely constant. Intuitively, the update is non‑trivial exactly when the old policy is not already proportional to the frozen‑future success factors.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Proof of <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Equivalence and corollaries ‣ 5 REMOVING INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We split the proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 5.9 (Optimisation pressure, thrice). ‣ 5.1 Equivalence and corollaries ‣ 5 REMOVING INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a> into several lemmas.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.8</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For any prior <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math>, non-positive reward function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, deterministic dynamics <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\alpha(k)}=\pi^{\mathcal{H}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha(k)}=\pi^{\mathcal{H}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(k)=2^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(k)=2^{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Throughout the proof, we will assume that the prior is uniform; otherwise the prior is folded into the reward. Let us first consider the case of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We have that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{(k)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\left(\frac{p(\mathcal{O}^{(k)}|a,s)p(a|s)}{p(\mathcal{O}^{(k)}|s)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\left(\frac{p(\mathcal{O}^{(k)}|a,s)p(a|s)}{p(\mathcal{O}^{(k)}|s)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r_{k}(s,a)+C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r_{k}(s,a)+C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the constant</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\log|A|-\log\frac{\sum_{a}\exp r_{k}(s,a)}{|A|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>a</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\log|A|-\log\frac{\sum_{a}\exp r_{k}(s,a)}{|A|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">does not depend on <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math>. We also observe that shifting reward by any additive constant does not change the policy (a soft version of the reward shaping lemma): for <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}(s,a)=r(s,a)+C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}(s,a)=r(s,a)+C</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex87.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{p(a|s)e^{r(s,a)+C}}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}p(a^{\prime}|s)e^{r(s,a)+C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{p(a|s)e^{r(s,a)+C}}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}p(a^{\prime}|s)e^{r(s,a)+C}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{p(a|s)e^{r(s,a)}}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}p(a^{\prime}|s)e^{r(s,a)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{p(a|s)e^{r(s,a)}}{\sum_{a^{\prime}}p(a^{\prime}|s)e^{r(s,a)}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">To ignore the constants, we write <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\equiv r^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≡</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\equiv r^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=r^{\prime}+C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=r^{\prime}+C</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the iterative process of adding the posterior to the reward results in a sequence:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{0}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{0}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex89.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv r(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv r(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{1}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{1}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex90.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv r_{0}(s,a)+\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv r_{0}(s,a)+\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv 2r(s,a)+C_{1}\equiv 2r(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv 2r(s,a)+C_{1}\equiv 2r(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{k}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{k}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex93.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv r_{k-1}(s,a)+\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{(k-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv r_{k-1}(s,a)+\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{(k-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv 2r_{k-1}(s,a)+C_{k}\equiv 2^{k}r(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv 2r_{k-1}(s,a)+C_{k}\equiv 2^{k}r(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">This proves, by induction on <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{H}}_{k}=\pi_{\alpha(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{H}}_{k}=\pi_{\alpha(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">The case of <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> is then done by backwards induction over the time horizon. We are given <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\leq t&lt;T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\leq t&lt;T</annotation></semantics></math> and we assume that the following inductive hypothesis holds for all <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;t^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;t^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and for all <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r_{k}(s,a)=2^{k}r_{0}(s,a)\qquad p(\mathcal{O}_{t^{\prime}:T}^{\alpha(k)}|s_{t^{\prime}})=p(\mathcal{O}_{t^{\prime}:T}^{(k)}|s_{t^{\prime}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi></msup><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}(s,a)=2^{k}r_{0}(s,a)\qquad p(\mathcal{O}_{t^{\prime}:T}^{\alpha(k)}|s_{t^{\prime}})=p(\mathcal{O}_{t^{\prime}:T}^{(k)}|s_{t^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">In case of the policy obtained by decreasing the temperature, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\alpha(k+1)}(a_{t}|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\alpha(k+1)}(a_{t}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex96.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p(a_{t}|s_{t},\mathcal{O}_{t:T}^{\alpha(k+1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p(a_{t}|s_{t},\mathcal{O}_{t:T}^{\alpha(k+1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}^{\alpha(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(a_{t}|s_{t})-\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}^{\alpha(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(a_{t}|s_{t})-\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t:T}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t}^{\alpha(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{\alpha(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t}^{\alpha(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{\alpha(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2^{k+1}r_{0}(a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{\alpha(k+1)}|s_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2^{k+1}r_{0}(a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{\alpha(k+1)}|s_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">where the first line follows from the definition, the next one from the Bayes’ law, the next one from the assumption that the prior is uniform, and the next one from the definition of the <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}_{1}^{\alpha(k+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}_{1}^{\alpha(k+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> and using the fact that there is a unique <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t+1}</annotation></semantics></math> which follows <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(a_{t},s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(a_{t},s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We look at the policy obtained by folding the posterior into the reward:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{(k+1)}^{\mathcal{H}}(a_{t}|s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{(k+1)}^{\mathcal{H}}(a_{t}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex100.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log p(a_{t}|s_{t},\mathcal{O}_{t:T}^{(k+1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log p(a_{t}|s_{t},\mathcal{O}_{t:T}^{(k+1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t}^{(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≡</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t}^{(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{(k+1)}|a_{t},s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=r_{k+1}(a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{(k+1)}|s_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r_{k+1}(a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{(k+1)}|s_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=2^{k+1}r_{0}(a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{\alpha(k+1)}|s_{t+1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2^{k+1}r_{0}(a_{t},s_{t})+\log p(\mathcal{O}_{t+1:T}^{\alpha(k+1)}|s_{t+1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last line follows from the inductive hypothesis.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.9</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For any prior <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math>, non-positive reward function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, arbitrary dynamics <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.Thmtheorem9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}=\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}=\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proof by induction on <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. Assume without loss of generality uniform prior <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise fold it into the reward. For <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0</annotation></semantics></math> they coincide by definition. Now, assume that <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}=\pi_{k}^{\mathcal{F}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}=\pi_{k}^{\mathcal{F}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we show the inductive step for <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k+1</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us denote the corresponding <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> functions by <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>.
First, exactly as in the proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem4" title="Proposition 5.4 (Strong return improvement lemma). ‣ 5 REMOVING INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.4</span></a>, we know that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k+1}^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})=\frac{\pi_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a|s_{t})]}\ \propto\ \pi_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mi>Q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k+1}^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})=\frac{\pi_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a_{t}|s_{t})}{\mathbb{E}_{a_{t}\sim\pi(\cdot|s_{t})}[\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a|s_{t})]}\ \propto\ \pi_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">and on the other hand, we also know from the definition that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k+1}^{\mathcal{F}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\ \propto\ p(s_{t}|a_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(a_{t}|s_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k+1}^{\mathcal{F}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\ \propto\ p(s_{t}|a_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(a_{t}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we aim to show that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s_{t}|a_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(a_{t}|s_{t})=C_{t}\pi_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a_{t}|s_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s_{t}|a_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(a_{t}|s_{t})=C_{t}\pi_{k}^{\mathcal{G}}(a_{t}|s_{t})\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a_{t}|s_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">up to some multiplicative constant <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We do this again by induction, this time on a time horizon <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Using <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 4.1 (Soft 𝑄 and 𝑉 functions). ‣ 4 THE THEORY OF INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(s_{T},a_{T})=\exp r_{k}(s_{T},a_{T})=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a_{T}|s_{T})\exp r_{0}(s_{T},a_{T})=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a_{T}|s_{T})\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(s_{T},a_{T})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(s_{T},a_{T})=\exp r_{k}(s_{T},a_{T})=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a_{T}|s_{T})\exp r_{0}(s_{T},a_{T})=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(a_{T}|s_{T})\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(s_{T},a_{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">which proves this in case <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=T</annotation></semantics></math>. Inductive step: assume that the hypothesis holds for <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t+1</annotation></semantics></math>, and write:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\exp V^{\mathcal{F}}(s_{t+1})=\mathbb{E}_{a_{t+1}\sim p}[\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(s_{t+1}(a_{t+1})]=\frac{C_{t}}{|A|}\mathbb{E}_{a_{t+1}\sim\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}}[\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(s_{t+1}(a_{t+1})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp V^{\mathcal{F}}(s_{t+1})=\mathbb{E}_{a_{t+1}\sim p}[\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(s_{t+1}(a_{t+1})]=\frac{C_{t}}{|A|}\mathbb{E}_{a_{t+1}\sim\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}}[\exp Q^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(s_{t+1}(a_{t+1})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A1.SS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>log</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log</annotation></semantics></math> and bringing the factor outside the expectation shows that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[\exp V^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(s_{t+1})]=\frac{C_{t}}{|A|}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[\exp V^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(s_{t+1})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[\exp V^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(s_{t+1})]=\frac{C_{t}}{|A|}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[\exp V^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(s_{t+1})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">which means:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(s_{t},a_{t})=\exp r_{k}(s_{t},a_{t})\cdot\frac{C_{t}}{|A|}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[\exp V^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(s_{t+1})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp Q^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}(s_{t},a_{t})=\exp r_{k}(s_{t},a_{t})\cdot\frac{C_{t}}{|A|}\mathbb{E}_{s_{t+1}}[\exp V^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}(s_{t+1})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">proving the lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.10</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
For any prior <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(a|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(a|s)</annotation></semantics></math>, non-positive reward function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, deterministic dynamics <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(s_{t+1}|s_{t},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> we have <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}=\pi_{\alpha(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{k}=\pi_{\alpha(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> for schedule <math id="A1.Thmtheorem10.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(k)=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(k)=k</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof follows almost exactly like the one in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem8" title="Lemma A.8. ‣ A.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix A PROOFS" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.8</span></a>. The base case is identical. In the inductive case, we write analogously:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{0}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{0}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv r(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv r(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{1}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{1}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex112.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv r_{0}(s,a)+\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv r_{0}(s,a)+\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv 2r(s,a)+C_{1}\equiv 2r(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv 2r(s,a)+C_{1}\equiv 2r(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\dots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\dots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright" colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r_{k}(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r_{k}(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex115.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv r_{0}(s,a)+\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{(k-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv r_{0}(s,a)+\log p(a|s,\mathcal{O}^{(k-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\equiv kr(s,a)+C_{k}\equiv kr(s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\equiv kr(s,a)+C_{k}\equiv kr(s,a)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">and the rest of the proof follows as before.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Proof of <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem10" title="Corollary 5.10 (Return improvement rate). ‣ 5.1 Equivalence and corollaries ‣ 5 REMOVING INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Corollary</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.10</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.11</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Given a function <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x)=f(\arg\max_{t}(f(t)+xg(t)))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x)=f(\arg\max_{t}(f(t)+xg(t)))</annotation></semantics></math> for some differentiable functions <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f,g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f,g</annotation></semantics></math>, the derivative of <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex117" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dh}{dx}=-\frac{f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}{f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dh}{dx}=-\frac{f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}{f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}(x)=\arg\max_{t}f(t)+xg(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}(x)=\arg\max_{t}f(t)+xg(t)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{*}(x)=\arg\max_{t}(f(t)+xg(t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{*}(x)=\arg\max_{t}(f(t)+xg(t))</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex118" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dt}\left(f(t)+xg(t)\right)\bigg|_{t=t^{*}(x)}=0=f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dt}\left(f(t)+xg(t)\right)\bigg|_{t=t^{*}(x)}=0=f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex119" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=-\frac{f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}{g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=-\frac{f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}{g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To differentiate <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the fact that <math id="A1.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h(x)=f(t^{*}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h(x)=f(t^{*}(x))</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives us:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex120" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dh}{dx}=\frac{d}{dx}f(t^{*}(x))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dh}{dx}=\frac{d}{dx}f(t^{*}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the chain rule:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex121" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dh}{dx}=f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))\cdot\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dh}{dx}=f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))\cdot\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">To find <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}</annotation></semantics></math>, we differentiate the first-order condition <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))=0</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A1.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dx}\left(f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))\right)=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dx}\left(f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))\right)=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the chain rule:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex123" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))\cdot\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}+g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))\cdot\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))\cdot\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}+g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))\cdot\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Rearrange to solve for <math id="A1.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex124" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))\right)\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}=-g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))\right)\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}=-g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex125" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}=-\frac{g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}{f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dt^{*}(x)}{dx}=-\frac{g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}{f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, substituting this back into the expression for <math id="A1.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dh}{dx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dh}{dx}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex126" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dh}{dx}=f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))\cdot\left(-\frac{g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}{f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dh}{dx}=f^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))\cdot\left(-\frac{g^{\prime}(t^{*}(x))}{f^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))+xg^{\prime\prime}(t^{*}(x))}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary A.12</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Return improvement rate)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In case of deterministic dynamics <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, given a sequence of policies <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> have that:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex127" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})-J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k-1})=\frac{1}{{k}}\cdot\frac{J^{\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})\cdot\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})}{J^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})+\frac{1}{{k}}\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})}+O\left(\frac{1}{{k}^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})-J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k-1})=\frac{1}{{k}}\cdot\frac{J^{\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})\cdot\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})}{J^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})+\frac{1}{{k}}\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})}+O\left(\frac{1}{{k}^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{H}}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{H}}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the causal entropy of policy <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, and the derivatives are taken with respect to the temperature <math id="A1.Thmtheorem12.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS4.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove this, we use an alternative characterization of the maximum entropy policies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haarnoja et al.,, 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Levine,, 2018</a>)</cite>. For a fixed temperature <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in\mathbb{R}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in\mathbb{R}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, the policy <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> maximizes the functional:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex128" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="J_{\alpha}(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{s_{t},a_{t}}[r(s_{t},a_{t})+\frac{1}{\alpha}\mathcal{H}(\pi(\cdot|s_{t}))]=J(\pi)+\frac{1}{\alpha}\hat{\mathcal{H}}(\pi)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>J</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\alpha}(\pi)=\mathbb{E}_{s_{t},a_{t}}[r(s_{t},a_{t})+\frac{1}{\alpha}\mathcal{H}(\pi(\cdot|s_{t}))]=J(\pi)+\frac{1}{\alpha}\hat{\mathcal{H}}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the expectation is taken over the trajectory induced by the policy <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\pi(\cdot|s))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\pi(\cdot|s))</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Shannon entropy of the policy in state <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the causal entropy of the policy <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the characterisation of the iterative retraining given by <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 5.9 (Optimisation pressure, thrice). ‣ 5.1 Equivalence and corollaries ‣ 5 REMOVING INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.9</span></a> we know that <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{j}=\pi_{\alpha(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>j</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{j}=\pi_{\alpha(j)}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.SS4.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(j)=j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(j)=j</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS4.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the Taylor expansion, for any twice-differentiable <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> we have:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex129" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\alpha+\eta)-u(\alpha)=\eta u^{\prime}(\alpha)+O(\eta^{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\alpha+\eta)-u(\alpha)=\eta u^{\prime}(\alpha)+O(\eta^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u(\alpha)=J(\arg\max_{\pi}J_{\frac{1}{\alpha}}(\pi))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>π</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u(\alpha)=J(\arg\max_{\pi}J_{\frac{1}{\alpha}}(\pi))</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k-1})-J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k-1})-J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex130.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=J(\pi_{\alpha(k-1)})-J(\pi_{\alpha(k)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=J(\pi_{\alpha(k-1)})-J(\pi_{\alpha(k)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u\left(\frac{1}{{k}}+\eta\right)-u\left(\frac{1}{{k}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u\left(\frac{1}{{k}}+\eta\right)-u\left(\frac{1}{{k}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\eta u^{\prime}\left(\frac{1}{{k}}\right)+O\left(\eta^{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\eta u^{\prime}\left(\frac{1}{{k}}\right)+O\left(\eta^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">for <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta=\frac{1}{k({k-1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta=\frac{1}{k({k-1})}</annotation></semantics></math>. Now, using <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem11" title="Lemma A.11. ‣ A.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix A PROOFS" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.11</span></a>, we derive:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex133" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}(x)=-\frac{J^{\prime}(\pi^{*}(x))\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime}(\pi^{*}(x))}{J^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{*}(x))+x\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{*}(x))}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}(x)=-\frac{J^{\prime}(\pi^{*}(x))\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime}(\pi^{*}(x))}{J^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{*}(x))+x\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{*}(x))}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">and substituting <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\frac{1}{{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\frac{1}{{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore <math id="A1.SS4.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{*}(x)=\pi_{\alpha(k)}=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{*}(x)=\pi_{\alpha(k)}=\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex134" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{\prime}(x)=-\frac{J^{\prime}(\pi_{\alpha(k)})\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime}(\pi_{\alpha(k)})}{J^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})+\frac{1}{{k}}\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime\prime}(\pi_{\alpha(k)})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{\prime}(x)=-\frac{J^{\prime}(\pi_{\alpha(k)})\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime}(\pi_{\alpha(k)})}{J^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})+\frac{1}{{k}}\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime\prime}(\pi_{\alpha(k)})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">which gives us the final equation:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex135" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})-J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k-1})=\frac{1}{{k}}\frac{J^{\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})}{J^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}))+\frac{1}{{k}}\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})}+O\left(\frac{1}{k}^{2}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msup><mi>J</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})-J(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k-1})=\frac{1}{{k}}\frac{J^{\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})}{J^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k}))+\frac{1}{{k}}\hat{\mathcal{H}}^{\prime\prime}(\pi^{\mathcal{G}}_{k})}+O\left(\frac{1}{k}^{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p10.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS4.p10.6.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>EXAMPLE  <a href="#Thmexample3" title="Example 3. ‣ 5.1 Equivalence and corollaries ‣ 5 REMOVING INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> EXPLICIT CALCULATION </h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Calculation for the <a href="#Thmexample3" title="Example 3. ‣ 5.1 Equivalence and corollaries ‣ 5 REMOVING INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> in detail.
<br class="ltx_break">We take a three-state, two action Markov decision process with initial state <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> and a uniform prior policy:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex136" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\pi(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\frac{1}{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\pi(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">with transition dynamics depicted on the diagram below:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex137" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.Ex137.m1.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="51.26" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-22.24px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 175.98 51.26" width="175.98"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,51.26) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(87.99,0) translate(0,26.39)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -87.99 -4.15)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 22.58)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 15.44)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(19.22,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -13.27 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="12.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{s_{1}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{s_{1}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 38.45 0) translate(49.54,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -10.38 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.06em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\emptyset}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\emptyset}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 104.33 0) translate(52.43,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -13.27 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.43em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.03" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 5.96)" width="12.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{s_{2}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{s_{2}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D65C5C;--ltx-fill-color:#D65C5C;--ltx-fg-color:#D65C5C;" color="#D65C5C" fill="#D65C5C" stroke="#D65C5C" stroke-dasharray="2.79985pt,1.59991pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -16.61 10.77 C -24.07 15.91 -44.7 15.91 -56.95 7.46"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-0.82315 -0.56783 0.56783 -0.82315 -57.18 7.3)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D65C5C;--ltx-fill-color:#D65C5C;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" fill="#D65C5C" stroke="#D65C5C" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -47.71 17.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.32em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.46)" width="9.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\color[rgb]{0.8392,0.3608,0.3608}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\frac{3}{4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle scriptlevel="+1"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#D65C5C;" mathcolor="#D65C5C"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#D65C5C;" mathcolor="#D65C5C">3</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#D65C5C;" mathcolor="#D65C5C">4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\color[rgb]{0.8392,0.3608,0.3608}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\frac{3}{4}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -13.87 -10.26 C -24.07 -17.3 -44.7 -17.3 -52.55 -11.88"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-0.82317 0.5678 -0.5678 -0.82317 -52.78 -11.72)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -38.86 -23.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.32em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.46)" width="9.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle scriptlevel="+1"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D65C5C;--ltx-fill-color:#D65C5C;--ltx-fg-color:#D65C5C;" color="#D65C5C" fill="#D65C5C" stroke="#D65C5C" stroke-dasharray="2.79985pt,1.59991pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 16.61 10.77 C 24.07 15.91 44.7 15.91 56.95 7.46"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.82315 -0.56783 0.56783 0.82315 57.18 7.3)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#D65C5C;--ltx-fill-color:#D65C5C;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" fill="#D65C5C" stroke="#D65C5C" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 38.3 17.43)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.32em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.46)" width="9.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\color[rgb]{0.8392,0.3608,0.3608}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\frac{1}{4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle scriptlevel="+1"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#D65C5C;" mathcolor="#D65C5C"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#D65C5C;" mathcolor="#D65C5C">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#D65C5C;" mathcolor="#D65C5C">4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\color[rgb]{0.8392,0.3608,0.3608}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\frac{1}{4}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 13.87 -10.26 C 24.07 -17.3 44.7 -17.3 52.55 -11.88"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.82317 0.5678 -0.5678 0.82317 52.78 -11.72)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 29.44 -23.41)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.68em;--ltx-fo-height:0.32em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="4.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 4.46)" width="9.42"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A2.Ex137.m1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle scriptlevel="+1"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\scriptstyle{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where red dotted lines correspond to action <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and solid black lines to action <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. We also assume that:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex138" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(s_{0},\cdot)=\log 1\qquad r(s_{1},\cdot)=\log\frac{1}{3}\qquad r(s_{2},\cdot)=\log\frac{2}{3}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(s_{0},\cdot)=\log 1\qquad r(s_{1},\cdot)=\log\frac{1}{3}\qquad r(s_{2},\cdot)=\log\frac{2}{3}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Control-as-inference operator</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The first iteration of <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(\cdot|\emptyset)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(\cdot|\emptyset)</annotation></semantics></math> computes the probability of getting reward for action <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex139" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{1},\emptyset)\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{3}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot\frac{2}{3}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{5}{24}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{1},\emptyset)\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{3}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot\frac{2}{3}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{5}{24}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and for <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex140" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{2}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{2},\emptyset)\mathbb{P}(a_{2}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{3}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{2}{3}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{6}{24}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{2}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{2},\emptyset)\mathbb{P}(a_{2}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{3}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{2}{3}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{6}{24}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">After normalisation, we get:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex141" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\frac{5}{11}\qquad\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\frac{6}{11}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\frac{5}{11}\qquad\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\frac{6}{11}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Now, applying the same computation second time - for <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex142" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{2}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{1},\emptyset)\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{1}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{5}{11}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{3}+\frac{5}{11}\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot\frac{2}{3}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{25}{11\cdot 12}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{2}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{1},\emptyset)\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{1}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{5}{11}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{3}+\frac{5}{11}\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot\frac{2}{3}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{25}{11\cdot 12}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">and for <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex143" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{2}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{2},\emptyset)\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{2}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{6}{11}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{3}+\frac{6}{11}\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot\frac{2}{3}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{36}{11\cdot 12}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{2}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{2},\emptyset)\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{2}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{6}{11}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{3}+\frac{6}{11}\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot\frac{2}{3}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{36}{11\cdot 12}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Again applying normalisation:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex144" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\frac{25}{61}\qquad\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\frac{36}{61}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>61</mn></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>36</mn><mn>61</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\frac{25}{61}\qquad\pi^{\mathcal{F}}_{1}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\frac{36}{61}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Raising temperature</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Raising temperature policy <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\alpha(2)}(\cdot|\emptyset)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha(2)}(\cdot|\emptyset)</annotation></semantics></math> first modifies the MDP by setting the rewards:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex145" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}(s_{1})=\log\frac{1}{9}\qquad r_{2}(s_{2})=\log\frac{4}{9}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}(s_{1})=\log\frac{1}{9}\qquad r_{2}(s_{2})=\log\frac{4}{9}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and then recomputes the posterior for <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex146" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\alpha(2)}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{1},\emptyset)\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{9}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot\frac{4}{9}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{7}{72}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>72</mn></mfrac><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha(2)}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{1},\emptyset)\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{1}{9}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{4}\cdot\frac{4}{9}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{7}{72}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex147" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{\alpha(2)}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{2},\emptyset)\mathbb{P}(a_{2}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{9}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{4}{9}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{10}{72}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>72</mn></mfrac><mo>/</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha(2)}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\mathbb{P}(a_{1}|\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2},\emptyset)=\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2}|a_{2},\emptyset)\mathbb{P}(a_{2}|\emptyset)}{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\left(\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{9}+\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{4}{9}\right)/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}=\frac{10}{72}/{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{O}^{2}_{1:2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Again applying normalisation:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex148" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\alpha(2)}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\frac{7}{17}\qquad\pi_{\alpha(2)}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\frac{10}{17}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>17</mn></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>17</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\alpha(2)}(a_{1}|\emptyset)=\frac{7}{17}\qquad\pi_{\alpha(2)}(a_{2}|\emptyset)=\frac{10}{17}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>ITERATED BOLTZMANN CONVERGENCE</h2>

<div id="Thmexample4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 4</span></span><span id="Thmexample4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Boltzmann-coherent mountain race)<span id="Thmexample4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmexample4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmexample4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let us revisit the <a href="#Thmexample1" title="Example 1 (Mountain race). ‣ 1 INTRODUCTION" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Example</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. We might compute the Boltzmann-coherent policy by using the construction from <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem9" title="Definition 4.9 (Iterated 𝑓-coherence). ‣ 4.1 Incoherence ‣ 4 THE THEORY OF INCOHERENCE" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F3.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="141.17" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 275.2 141.17" width="275.2"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,141.17) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(8.07,0) translate(0,70.59)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.46 -4.8)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.06em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.15" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="A3.F3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\emptyset}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\emptyset}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 66.01 34.64)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:2.66em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="36.81"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<div id="A3.F3.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:26.6pt;height:13.7pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(6.6pt,-3.4pt) scale(2.0,2.0) ;">
<div id="A3.F3.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:0.0pt;height:10.3pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,-1.7pt) scale(1.5,1.5) ;">
